@startuml backend-clean-architecture-rings
title agentd backend — clean architecture: every dependency points INWARD

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

package "PRESENTATION — transport / adapters (outer ring)" as PRES #EAF3FF {
  rectangle "gateway.py\n--\nWebSocket frames, auth + origin/scope gates,\nmethod dispatch, broadcast events out" as GW
}

package "APPLICATION — use cases (the recipe)" as APP #F0FFF0 {
  rectangle "AgentService.handle_message\n--\norchestration ONLY, imports no I/O libraries\n(the conductor: decides the order of work)" as SVC
  rectangle "interfaces/  (Protocols = promises)\n--\nAgentEngine · AgentRegistry\nSessionStore · EventSink" as PORTS
}

package "DOMAIN — pure rules + value objects (center)" as DOM #FFF7E6 {
  rectangle "agent.py: AgentSpec · select_tools · apply_mode\nmessages.py: UserMessage · Message\n--\nno disk, no network, no framework imports\n(same answer on a machine with no I/O)" as D
}

package "INFRASTRUCTURE — the machinery" as INF #FFF0F0 {
  rectangle "NativeEngine (the reason->act loop, native.py)\nFileAgentRegistry (reads agents/<id>/ off disk)\nJSON SessionStore (transcript on disk)\nLiteLLM adapter (the model call)" as I
}

rectangle "main/container.py — COMPOSITION ROOT\n--\nthe ONE place allowed to know every concrete class.\nConstructs the infra objects and INJECTS them into\nAgentService at boot. Swap an impl here, nothing else moves." as CR #F5F0FF

' ---- dependency arrows: which file KNOWS ABOUT which (imports/calls) ----
GW --> SVC   : uses the use case
GW ..>  D    : reads AgentSpec / RunMode
SVC --> D    : applies domain rules
SVC --> PORTS: depends on PROMISES,\nnot on concrete infra
I ..|> PORTS : implements\n(dependency INVERSION)
I -->  D     : builds / uses domain objects
CR ..> I     : constructs the impls
CR ..> SVC   : injects them

note right of INF
  Read the arrows: EVERY one points toward the center (Domain).
  Infrastructure's arrow into the ports is a dashed "implements":
  it FULFILLS a promise the application defines. So the *code
  dependency* points inward even though *data* flows outward at
  run time. That inversion is the whole trick — it lets you
  replace NativeEngine, the registry, or the store without the
  application or domain changing a single line.
end note

note bottom of DOM
  Why the center is "scary but safe": it holds the most RULES
  (the valuable part), but the LEAST machinery. A pure function
  can only return a wrong list — a unit test catches that in a
  millisecond. It can't corrupt a file or hang a socket.
end note
@enduml


@startuml backend-clean-architecture-flow
title A message from the desktop app, end to end — the trip IN and the trip OUT

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
  DividerBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

participant "Desktop app\n(agentd-client.js)" as C

box "PRESENTATION — transport only" #EAF3FF
  participant "gateway.py\n_handle_conn / _dispatch\n_chat_send / _run" as GW
end box

box "APPLICATION — the recipe" #F0FFF0
  participant "AgentService\nhandle_message" as SVC
end box

box "DOMAIN — pure rules (no I/O)" #FFF7E6
  participant "agent.py\nselect_tools\napply_mode" as DOM
end box

box "INFRASTRUCTURE — the machinery" #FFF0F0
  participant "Infra adapters\n(registry · session\n· prompt)" as ADP
  participant "NativeEngine\nrun_agent_loop" as ENG
  participant "LiteLLM\n+ tools" as LLM
end box

== TRIP IN : the request falls inward, ring by ring ==

C -> GW : chat.send frame (WebSocket)\n{sessionKey, message, agentId}
activate GW
GW -> GW : _handle_conn: parse_frame,\nauth + origin/scope gate
GW -> GW : _chat_send: validate,\nspawn _run background task
GW --> C : {runId} — returns IMMEDIATELY\n(the turn keeps running in the background)

note over GW: _run defines on_event (the EventSink),\nthen HANDS OFF. It knows nothing of tools or the LLM.
GW -> SVC : handle_message(message, on_event, abort)
activate SVC
note over GW, SVC #FFFBE6: BOUNDARY presentation -> application.\non_event is passed DOWN as a callback (the EventSink interface) —\nthat callback is how the answer will climb back out later.

SVC -> DOM : select_tools(catalog, spec)\napply_mode(tools, mode)
activate DOM
DOM --> SVC : the tools THIS agent may use
deactivate DOM
note over DOM #FFFBE6: PURE. No disk, no network. The center of the onion —\nthe valuable, unit-testable core. Request has reached the middle.

SVC -> ADP : registry.get(id) · session.load()\nbuild_prompt(...)
activate ADP
ADP --> SVC : AgentSpec · prior history · system prompt
deactivate ADP
note over SVC, ADP #FFFBE6: These are INTERFACE calls (promises). The concrete\nimpls (file registry, JSON store) were injected by the\ncomposition root at boot — the service never named them.

SVC -> ENG : engine.run(messages, prompt, tools, on_event)
activate ENG

== THE LOOP : infrastructure does the real work ==

loop until the model stops asking for tools
  ENG -> LLM : stream completion
  LLM --> ENG : assistant text + tool calls
  ENG ->> GW : on_event(message_end)
  note right of GW: streamed to the client live (below)
  opt tool calls present
    ENG -> LLM : execute the tool(s)
    LLM --> ENG : tool result
    ENG ->> GW : on_event(tool_result)
    ENG -> ENG : feed result back,\nloop again
  end
end

== TRIP OUT : events stream outward via the callback ==

note over ENG, GW #FFFBE6: The inner loop never RETURNS the answer. It calls on_event —\na callback the OUTER layer handed in. Infrastructure stays\nblind to the WebSocket; presentation owns "how to reach the client."
ENG ->> GW : on_event(agent_end)
deactivate ENG
deactivate SVC
GW -> GW : _broadcast -> _send_all\n(wrap each event as a chat.event frame)
GW ->> C : chat.event frames (streamed)
deactivate GW
note over C: the desktop renders tokens as they arrive,\nfiltering by runId / agentId. Swap it for a phone\nor a Slack bot and nothing inside the rings changes.

note across #F5F0FF
  Who decided ADP = FileAgentRegistry, ENG = NativeEngine, LLM = LiteLLM?
  main/container.py (the COMPOSITION ROOT) — the single place that knows
  every concrete class and injects them behind the interfaces above.
end note
@enduml
